# Template of a site file for another app on the rt server (docs/ops.md '새 앱 추가').
# Copy it to /etc/caddy/sites/<app>.caddy (the name must end in .caddy; this file does not, so
# Caddy never loads it), then replace the address and the port from the port table.
# - No `log` directive: no access log, so no client IP addresses (the server-wide filter in
#   /etc/caddy/Caddyfile cleans the error log).
# - No `trusted_proxies`: X-Forwarded-For is always the real client address.
# - The app listens on 127.0.0.1 only; Caddy is the only way in.
# - stream_close_delay (recommended): open WebSockets survive a Caddy reload for up to 5 minutes
#   instead of being closed at once.
app.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3500 {
		stream_close_delay 5m
	}
}
